cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
title: "PrismFlow: Dependence-Discounted Evidential Fusion under Collusive View Compromise"
abstract: >-
  A multi-view learning research project testing the hypothesis that agreement
  between views should contribute evidence in proportion to the effective
  independence of those views, not in proportion to how many views agree. The
  detection half of the hypothesis is supported and the defence half is
  refuted as tested; no calibration metric has been computed on real retrieved
  evidence. See docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md for what is evidenced, what is not, and
  what was never measured.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kumar
    given-names: Mudit
date-released: 2026-10-07
keywords:
  - multi-view learning
  - evidential deep learning
  - uncertainty calibration
  - view dependence
  - effective number of independent views
